## Summary
The article discusses the enduring humor of the 46-year-old comedy film 'Airplane!', which remains funny over decades due to its deadpan style of playing everything straight. It highlights how the film defines a unique genre and appeals to new generations of viewers.

## Key Points
- 'Airplane!' continues to be humorous and grows funnier with time despite its age.
- The film's comedy relies on a serious, straight-faced approach to absurd situations, creating rapid-fire deadpan jokes.
- It is considered a genre-defining work in comedy that influences modern perceptions of humor.
- Younger audiences who missed its original release still find it funny and appreciate its impact.
- The article references a philosophical perspective (Benjaminian view) on timeless works like 'Airplane!'.


